<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 70,369 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 70,369 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 70,369 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Thursday compared to 65,600 tonnes in the same period on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Thursday    March 12</p>
<p>    Export cargo		19,903	23,425</p>
<p>    Import cargo		50,466	42,175</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and five are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		72,876	 Johar		  13/3</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasen Courage    15/3</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-I	    15/3</p>
<p>Vehicles		    107	 Arcadia Highway    16/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
